# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY: scripts/validate.py fingerprints baseline.json BYTES (SHA1 hex-12).
# A CRLF flip changes the bytes and breaks the fingerprint. On Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, newly materialized files get CRLF — so force LF for
# JSON everywhere. Markdown and other text keep Git's default handling
# (nothing hashes their bytes).
*.json text eol=lf
